# Production dependency vulnerability allowlist
# Only for upstream issues with no available fix or legitimate blockers.
# Each numeric line: advisory source ID (from npm audit --json).
# Each group MUST have a "# BLOCKER: <reason>" line in its comment block;
# the audit script (.ci/scripts/security/audit.sh) enforces this strictly.

# astro <6.1.6 XSS in define:vars via incomplete </script> sanitization
# (GHSA-j687-52p2-xcff; fix requires Astro 6.x major)
# A sibling re-issue (1116896) existed across the GitHub Advisory Database
# split; it no longer appears in npm audit output and has been pruned.
# BLOCKER: astro 6 is a major migration tracked separately; the marketing site
# is statically pre-rendered (output: 'static') and only the locale-prefixed
# routes from getStaticPaths() are emitted, so define:vars in BaseLayout.astro
# never serializes a runtime-attacker-controlled pathname — Cloudflare Workers
# returns 404 for any path Astro didn't bake at build time
1117141

# astro <6.1.10 server island encrypted-parameter cross-component replay
# (GHSA-xr5h-phrj-8vxv; fix requires Astro 6.x major)
# BLOCKER: same astro 6 major migration as 1117141; server islands are
# disabled in our static-output marketing site (no SSR endpoints emit encrypted
# Astro.props blobs), so the cross-component replay surface is not present at
# runtime; revisit when @astrojs/mdx unblocks the Astro 6 upgrade
1118920

# esbuild 0.27.7 (GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr low), fixed in 0.28.1. A sibling high
# advisory (1120679) no longer appears in npm audit output and was pruned.
# Pulled transitively by astro@5.18.1 (esbuild ^0.27.3) and vite@7.3.3 (esbuild ^0.27.0);
# 0.28.1 is outside both ^0.27.x carets, so reaching the fix needs a forced override that
# overrides astro's pinned peer range and risks an esbuild 0.28 www-build regression.
# BLOCKER: neither advisory is reachable in our build — the high one is the esbuild Deno module (lib/deno/mod.ts), which we never import (Node-only toolchain), and the low one is the esbuild dev server's Windows path traversal; the dev server is never shipped to prod and CI/prod builds do not run on Windows. Drop once astro/vite widen the esbuild range to admit 0.28.1.
1120680

# astro 5.18.1 reflected-XSS / unescaped-attribute / host-header SSRF advisories
# (1120912, 1120917; sibling 1120914 no longer fires and was pruned). The patched
# versions are astro 7.0.2+, a major upgrade that removes legacy content collections
# and requires migrating src/content/config.ts to src/content.config.ts with
# collection loaders — a breaking change across the docs site, tracked separately.
# BLOCKER: @rediacc/www builds with astro output: 'static'; the slot-name XSS,
# spread-attribute XSS, and prerendered error-page SSRF paths are all SSR/host-header
# paths that do not exist in a static export. Drop once the site migrates to astro v7.
1120912
1120917

# js-yaml 3.x quadratic CPU in !!omap resolution (GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj,
# CVE-2026-59870). The 4.x half of this advisory was FIXED, not allowlisted:
# the root override moved >=4.2.0 <5.0.0 -> >=4.3.1 <5.0.0, which cleared
# sibling id 1138115 and every 4.x consumer (astro, @astrojs/markdown-remark,
# @marp-team/marpit all resolve 4.3.1 now). Only the 3.x instance is left.
# BLOCKER: no patched 3.x exists — the advisory states the fix was NOT
# backported — and the single consumer cannot move to 4.x: gray-matter@4.0.3
# binds yaml.safeLoad/safeDump (lib/engines.js:16-17), both REMOVED in js-yaml
# 4, which is why the nested "gray-matter": {"js-yaml": "^3.15.0"} override
# already exists. Not reachable as a DoS either: gray-matter is a build-time
# dependency of packages/www only (npm ls shows @rediacc/www as its sole
# parent), it parses frontmatter of our own committed content, and www is
# output: 'static' (astro.config.mjs:144) so no server evaluates YAML at
# request time. Re-check when gray-matter ships a js-yaml 4 engine.
1138114
